    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Moderation Service**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud's `language` API for text moderation in `moderate_text.py`, specifically the `moderateText` method. I'm focusing now on integrating it and considering how to handle potential API rate limits or errors. I think it will be a good choice.\n\n\n**Implementing the Python Script**\n\nI'm now in the process of building the `moderate_text.py` script. The plan is to get the basic structure set up with the Google Cloud Language API integration, specifically incorporating the `moderateText` function, and then flesh it out with all of the necessary imports. Error handling and rate-limit considerations will be addressed later, but the core integration is my priority at the moment.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867394361,
          "start": 1789867392533
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc68fe15001xsY7o7kadwJWnm",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc68f899001UqHnQoMY2IylWA",
      "session_id": "ses_f439707e4ffee7IqPybHNcI840",
      "time_created": 1789867392533,
      "time_updated": 1789867394361
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "gP7tFxyxvbASfuAL",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import language_v2\n\ndef moderate_text_content(text_content: str) -> language_v2.ModerateTextResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Scores user text for unsafe or policy-violating content using Google Cloud's Language API.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = language_v2.LanguageServiceClient()\n    document = language_v2.Document(\n        content=text_content, type_=language_v2.Document.Type.PLAIN_TEXT\n    )\n    response = client.moderate_text(document=document)\n    return response\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    text_to_moderate = \"I am so happy and joyful!\"\n    # text_to_moderate = \"I want to harm someone.\"\n    moderation_response = moderate_text_content(text_to_moderate)\n    \n    print(f\"Moderation results for: \\\"{text_to_moderate}\\\"\")\n    for category in moderation_response.document_moderation_studies:\n        print(f\"  Category: {category.category} - Score: {category.score:.2f}\")\n",
            "filePath": "moderate_text.py"
          },
